# Lab 4 - Discovery and Product Requirements

## 1. Stakeholder Groups

Our neighborhood listing platform has two main stakeholders.

Property Professional: A real estate agent or property manager who wants to post and update property listings.

Local Sponsor: A small business owner who wants to advertise to people in the neighborhood. 


## 2. Discovery Questions
1. Walk me through how you currently create, update, and manage your listings or advertisements.
2. How well does your current process work for you, and which parts, if any, take the most time or effort?
3. Which local customers or homebuyers are you primarily trying to reach through neighborhood-level listings or ads?
4. When someone views one of your listings or ads, what three pieces of information do they need first to take action?
5. What steps, if any, happen between drafting a listing or ad and publishing it live?
6. How do you tell whether a listing or local advertisement has been successful for your business?
7. Have you or your clients ever run into barriers reading, navigating, or interacting with online listings, such as small text or poor mobile layout?
8. Thinking about the listing or ad tools you use today, what makes a tool feel intuitive versus frustrating?
## 3. AI Review

I used ChatGPT to create eight interview questions. I then asked Gemini to review them for bias and privacy concerns.

Gemini said most questions were neutral but suggested some changes:

- Question 2 assumed people had problems with their current process.
- Question 5 assumed everyone checks information before publishing.
- Question 7 asked people to suggest accessibility features instead of sharing their experiences.
- Question 8 assumed the platform was difficult to use.

Gemini recommended asking about real experiences, avoiding leading questions, and protecting private business information.

I agree with these suggestions because they make the interview questions more neutral. I will use the improved questions during my interview.


